Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/cofflink.c
Line: 1257
Function: get_name
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: Parses tokens from a raw section buffer without any bounds check: while (*ptr && *ptr != ' ') dereferences beyond the end of the allocated [copy, e) buffer when there is no terminating space or NUL in-range. In process_embedded_commands(), get_name is called with pointers into the .drectve section which is not guaranteed to be NUL-terminated, enabling an OOB read on crafted input.

